 "section_summary": "This section contains U.S. State Department and Embassy Rome correspondence from July to September 1946 regarding the custody and disposition of property and archives of the former Japanese Embassy in Italy. It documents inquiries into powers of attorney granted to Italian custodian Giulio Dante, coordination with SCAP in Tokyo, and microfilming requests before the redeployment of Nisei Army personnel. The section is dominated by Rome Despatch 3823 and its extensive itemized catalog of Japanese Embassy archives compiled by a six-man Nisei team.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "Urgent request to verify powers of attorney issued to Giulio Dante for custody of Japanese Embassy property in Rome.",
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1946-07-16",
