   "start_page": 8,
   "summary": "David McK. Key transmits an itemized catalog of over 1,500 items from the former Japanese Embassy archives in Rome, compiled and categorized by a six-man Nisei military team. The despatch notes the collection consists mostly of printed Japanese-language materials of minimal intelligence value and requests instructions on final disposition. It urges prompt microfilming requests before the Nisei soldiers are redeployed.",
